<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to offer 3-yr bonds of HUF 15 bln on May 8.</title>
<headline>Hungary to offer 3-yr bonds of HUF 15 bln on May 8.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 15 billion forint worth of the three-year government bonds of 2000/E series on May 8, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Monday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest    18 April 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 May 2000</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	 15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Maximum yield		17.86 pct</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	  97.33 pct</p>
<p>Average yield at last</p>
<p>	 auction (April 7)</p>
<p>	 2000/D bond	     17.36 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction		   98.37 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.00 percent, payable semi-anually starting from November 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
